  "original_parameters_and_hypotheses": [
    "The unchanged current production MediumAdmissible b sigma kappa c0 atom, used only to derive genuine alpha/gamma2/gamma3 one-boundedness and to construct poissonAtlasBlock.",
    "Actual source key k, activeD membership hd, q piece j:Fin 3, sign negative:Bool, Csep and arbitrary original Rectangle R.",
    "The source finite identities are valid for every z,y; interpretation as original inclusive rough cutoff uses the predecessor z>=0 and y=roughY(x) bridge.",
    "Generic B.atom=atom identity appears only in reusable upper-source lemma; the original caller discharges it by rfl, not by a SourceBind premise.",
    "No Hermitian symmetry, SW-after-polarization, spectral bound, variation bound or final medium target appears as a premise."
  ],
  "eliminated_obligations": [
    "Ordered complex polarization for three separate coefficient pairs, normalized by 2 per diagonal sequence, with exact l1 coefficient mass 4^3=64.",
    "Actual globally one-bounded diagonal coefficient sequences derived from current production alpha/gamma2/gamma3 support hypotheses; no outside-support bounds assumed.",
    "Each actual G signed upper-product term expands into the actual 64 diagonal finite source sums, with both independent st=d choices and original individual windows retained.",
    "The two smooth labels are frozen by an exhaustive disjoint finite regrouping over images of the actual choicesWithoutProductWindow, and each label satisfies st=d and both original y trims.",
    "Original poissonAtlasBlock.rectangleSum connects to all four signed upper-product terms with unchanged physical inverse phase and q*w1*w2 denominator.",
    "Explicit native counting-scale bound: norm original rectangleSum <=64*(mass_UU+mass_LU+mass_UL+mass_LL); each mass is the actual fibre-cardinality product divided by q*w1*w2, summed on the actual carrier. This is only the polarization/source counting envelope."
  ],
  "remaining_internal_obligations": [
